  "//states": "A SNAKE IS PRONE BY NATURE: `always` matches unconditionally, so the body is laid on the fitted ground plane (SettleClipOwnedBody) and every segment follows its own stretch of it (ConformProneSegments), the same two stages a legless zombie's crawl uses. bodyYOffset -0.65 lays it INTO the fitted plane: the prone placement holds a body's lowest collider corner half a voxel proud (kProneEmbedVox), which on a body 1.1 voxels thick is a snake hovering a hand above the ground (the snake gate measured 0.62..0.92 voxels of clearance at 0).",
  "states": [
    {
      "name": "slither",
      "always": true,
      "disableGait": true,
      "groundAlign": 1,
      "speedScale": 1,
      "lungeScale": 1,
      "bodyYOffset": -0.65
    }
  ],
